WEBVTT

1
00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:52.623
Subtitles by <font color="#ff0000">explosiveskull</font>
Sync by <font color="#00ffff">GoldenBeard</font>

2
00:01:17.694 --> 00:01:19.629
Quiet!

3
00:01:27.537 --> 00:01:29.603
What are you?

4
00:01:29.605 --> 00:01:31.738
Shh.

5
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.676
Oh.

6
00:01:47.757 --> 00:01:49.490
You're a demon!

7
00:01:49.492 --> 00:01:51.491
No, no. I'm not a demon.

8
00:01:51.493 --> 00:01:52.993
I'm not a demon.

9
00:01:52.995 --> 00:01:54.829
See? Just a guy.

10
00:01:54.831 --> 00:01:57.532
Just a guy here to rescue
these dragons, so, uh...

11
00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.901
- But you walked through fire!
- Dragon scales!

12
00:01:59.903 --> 00:02:01.135
Dragons shed a lot.

13
00:02:01.137 --> 00:02:03.136
No, I know a demon
when I see one.

14
00:02:03.138 --> 00:02:04.672
No human legs are that skinny.

15
00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:09.209
Think that's a good entrance?
Get a load of me.

16
00:02:11.814 --> 00:02:13.915
I knew it! More demons!

17
00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:15.483
Ah, it's really just a nitwit

18
00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:16.784
who forgot
to fireproof his butt.

19
00:02:16.786 --> 00:02:18.119
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

20
00:02:18.121 --> 00:02:19.821
Guys, no, not yet!

21
00:02:21.457 --> 00:02:23.990
- Behold, your worst nightmare.
- Behold.

22
00:02:23.992 --> 00:02:26.693
Along with his sister,
who insisted on coming.

23
00:02:26.695 --> 00:02:28.228
That's my intro?

24
00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.764
Guys, too soon.
You always come in too soon.

25
00:02:32.735 --> 00:02:35.602
Sorry, still getting
the hang of my wings.

26
00:02:35.604 --> 00:02:37.471
Fishlegs, again with the baby?

27
00:02:38.842 --> 00:02:40.674
- This is a raid.
- I couldn't find a sitter.

28
00:02:40.676 --> 00:02:42.677
Demons everywhere!

29
00:02:42.679 --> 00:02:44.779
It's the end of the world!

30
00:02:46.616 --> 00:02:49.549
Astrid. I had him
right where I wanted him.

31
00:02:49.551 --> 00:02:51.651
And now he's right
where I wanted him.

32
00:02:51.653 --> 00:02:52.820
Let's get to work.

33
00:02:52.822 --> 00:02:54.721
Okay, we screwed that up,

34
00:02:54.723 --> 00:02:58.059
but at least nobody else
knows we're here.

35
00:03:00.163 --> 00:03:02.697
Easy, girl. It's okay.

36
00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.566
We're gonna get you
out of here.

37
00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.937
A Crimson Goregutter!

38
00:03:16.846 --> 00:03:18.645
Look at this weirdo.

39
00:03:18.647 --> 00:03:20.180
Bet it's super-dumb.

40
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.817
Why can't I get this cage open?

41
00:03:23.819 --> 00:03:25.151
It slides.

42
00:03:25.153 --> 00:03:26.620
Obviously.

43
00:03:26.622 --> 00:03:28.256
Attack!

44
00:03:28.258 --> 00:03:31.258
- Get the rescues out of here!
- Get that Night Fury!

45
00:03:35.931 --> 00:03:37.631
No running on the deck!

46
00:03:37.633 --> 00:03:39.132
It's slippery.
You could fall.

47
00:03:39.134 --> 00:03:41.802
Step aside! Let me handle
the tough guy stuff.

48
00:03:42.838 --> 00:03:44.071
- Huh?
- Whoa.

49
00:03:45.741 --> 00:03:48.743
Yeah! That's two for me.

50
00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.114
Look out!

51
00:03:53.116 --> 00:03:55.149
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no!
- Sorry!

52
00:04:00.856 --> 00:04:03.624
Ha!

53
00:04:03.626 --> 00:04:05.059
Thank you.

54
00:04:05.061 --> 00:04:07.060
Now, go get the rest, bud.

55
00:04:09.064 --> 00:04:11.197
I thought this was supposed
to be a stealth mission.

56
00:04:11.199 --> 00:04:12.833
Yeah, they always
start that way.

57
00:04:12.835 --> 00:04:15.036
Look out!

58
00:04:16.738 --> 00:04:18.072
Thanks, Stormfly!

59
00:04:20.043 --> 00:04:21.942
Oh, stop worrying.

60
00:04:21.944 --> 00:04:23.610
They'll get it.

61
00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:29.183
Eventually.

62
00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:31.586
Move out! We got 'em all.

63
00:04:31.588 --> 00:04:33.721
I'm gonna headlock every last one of you.

64
00:04:33.723 --> 00:04:36.156
I might even leg-lock you.

65
00:04:36.158 --> 00:04:37.925
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!
- Amateurs.

66
00:04:37.927 --> 00:04:39.894
- I was just getting started.
- Clear out, guys!

67
00:04:39.896 --> 00:04:41.228
Go, go!

68
00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.165
Don't let them get away!

69
00:04:47.202 --> 00:04:48.803
Good hustle, boys!

70
00:04:51.374 --> 00:04:53.844
Toothless, time to go!

71
00:04:59.281 --> 00:05:00.848
Oh.

72
00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:04.017
Hey, guys.

73
00:05:07.923 --> 00:05:10.824
You always have my back, bud.

74
00:05:26.875 --> 00:05:31.312
This is Berk,
your new home away from home.

75
00:05:31.314 --> 00:05:32.680
A stunning, one-stop,

76
00:05:32.682 --> 00:05:35.382
all-expense-paid
dream destination.

77
00:05:36.952 --> 00:05:40.687
So, settle in and let
your worries melt away.

78
00:05:40.689 --> 00:05:44.827
The service here soars,
the cuisine is fiery...

79
00:05:46.928 --> 00:05:49.430
...and the locals are
as colorful as you get.

80
00:05:49.432 --> 00:05:53.401
Any run-of-the-mill paradise
boasts beaches and sunshine.

81
00:05:55.038 --> 00:05:56.003
Well, not us.

82
00:05:56.005 --> 00:05:59.440
We've got something
no one else can touch.

83
00:05:59.442 --> 00:06:02.976
- We, my friend, have dragons.
- Make room!

84
00:06:02.978 --> 00:06:03.978
They're coming!

85
00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:07.748
Lots and lots of dragons.

86
00:06:16.158 --> 00:06:18.692
Gang, meet our latest Berkians.

87
00:06:20.228 --> 00:06:22.796
Welcome to paradise, mate.

88
00:06:22.798 --> 00:06:25.733
- Our home is your home.
- Well, aren't you a beauty!

89
00:06:25.735 --> 00:06:27.267
- Ah, you're welcome. You're welcome.
- Ah.

90
00:06:27.269 --> 00:06:29.135
I took on, like,
a hundred trappers.

91
00:06:29.137 --> 00:06:30.471
A-a thousand trappers.

92
00:06:30.473 --> 00:06:32.305
All with burning undies.

93
00:06:32.307 --> 00:06:35.308
My thick, full beard almost caught on fire.

94
00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:38.079
Ugh. Just-just stop.

95
00:06:38.081 --> 00:06:39.413
So, uh, Hiccup's mom,

96
00:06:39.415 --> 00:06:41.214
any notes on
my bone-crushing assault,

97
00:06:41.216 --> 00:06:43.117
or was it pretty much perfect?

98
00:06:43.119 --> 00:06:45.853
Oh, it was indescribable.

99
00:06:45.855 --> 00:06:48.822
And please, call me Valka.
It has been a year.

100
00:06:48.824 --> 00:06:50.957
First-name basis.

101
00:06:50.959 --> 00:06:53.159
I think the real hero
of the day was Toothless.

102
00:06:53.161 --> 00:06:54.861
Isn't that right, bud?

103
00:06:54.863 --> 00:06:57.397
What would we do without you,
oh, king of dragons?

104
00:06:57.399 --> 00:06:59.099
What would we do?

105
00:06:59.101 --> 00:07:01.735
Well, we could train
a lot harder, for one.

106
00:07:01.737 --> 00:07:03.404
That was pretty sloppy.

107
00:07:03.406 --> 00:07:06.207
Astrid, uh, does have a point.

108
00:07:06.209 --> 00:07:09.810
Perhaps you all rely a little
bit too much on your dragons

109
00:07:09.812 --> 00:07:11.945
and not enough on one another.

110
00:07:11.947 --> 00:07:13.447
See? That's exactly
what I was saying.

111
00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:15.449
Just listen up, guys.

112
00:07:15.451 --> 00:07:17.985
Yeah, your mom's
super impressed with me.

113
00:07:17.987 --> 00:07:19.786
I'm like the son
she always wanted.

114
00:07:19.788 --> 00:07:21.322
Fishmeat.

115
00:07:21.324 --> 00:07:23.990
You found a new friend.

116
00:07:28.064 --> 00:07:29.304
- Mind your heads!
- Whoa! - Oh!

117
00:07:46.848 --> 00:07:50.384
What good is having
the king of dragons around

118
00:07:50.386 --> 00:07:52.252
if he can't keep the order?

119
00:07:52.254 --> 00:07:55.022
Hey, bud, do you want
to do something here or...?

120
00:08:01.963 --> 00:08:04.365
And where do you suppose
we put these ones?

121
00:08:04.367 --> 00:08:05.865
Ah, we'll make room.

122
00:08:07.302 --> 00:08:10.271
You brought back a Hobgobbler!

123
00:08:10.273 --> 00:08:13.440
They're a bad omen.
We're cursed.

124
00:08:13.442 --> 00:08:14.974
Nonsense.

125
00:08:14.976 --> 00:08:17.545
What harm could he do?

126
00:08:17.547 --> 00:08:18.646
No injuries.

127
00:08:18.648 --> 00:08:21.548
They're all a little shaken
but otherwise healthy.

128
00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.584
Now, who's hungry?

129
00:08:28.824 --> 00:08:32.059
Point is you can't keep
bringing dragons back here.

130
00:08:32.061 --> 00:08:34.060
Come on, boy.

131
00:08:34.062 --> 00:08:35.595
You're just asking for trouble.

132
00:08:35.597 --> 00:08:37.363
No, you don't,
you little thief!

133
00:08:37.365 --> 00:08:39.900
Those trappers are
getting closer by the day.

134
00:08:39.902 --> 00:08:42.069
We can handle them.
We have the alpha.

135
00:08:42.071 --> 00:08:43.570
Ain't that right, bud?

136
00:08:43.572 --> 00:08:45.339
Would you look at
how happy they are?

137
00:08:46.142 --> 00:08:49.075
She's awesome.

138
00:08:49.077 --> 00:08:51.445
Gobber, relax. We did it.

139
00:08:51.447 --> 00:08:54.047
The world's first
dragon-Viking utopia.

140
00:08:54.049 --> 00:08:55.583
We made the dream a reality.

141
00:08:55.585 --> 00:08:58.953
Your dream maybe.
Mine's less crowded and more...

142
00:09:00.623 --> 00:09:02.488
...sanitary.

143
00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.391
Gobber, you're not
fooling anybody.

144
00:09:04.393 --> 00:09:05.626
I know you love them.

145
00:09:10.265 --> 00:09:12.398
You're supposed to be
the generation

146
00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.868
that leads us into the future.

147
00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.871
Food fight!

148
00:09:16.873 --> 00:09:20.206
Ooh, gorgeous.

149
00:09:20.208 --> 00:09:22.209
- Watch the hair!
- Good, Fishmeat.

150
00:09:24.279 --> 00:09:27.046
- Ugh! God help us.
- Right between the eyes!

151
00:09:27.048 --> 00:09:29.650
Time to stop worrying about
problems out there...

152
00:09:29.652 --> 00:09:31.651
- Gobber.
- ...and start sorting out the ones right here.

153
00:09:31.653 --> 00:09:33.119
Okay, okay.

154
00:09:33.121 --> 00:09:34.354
I-I'll think about it.

155
00:09:34.356 --> 00:09:37.156
Hang up those saddles
and get married.

156
00:09:37.158 --> 00:09:39.493
The "M" word.

157
00:09:39.495 --> 00:09:42.595
Gross. Unless it's me.

158
00:09:42.597 --> 00:09:46.099
Start ruling like
a proper royal couple.

159
00:09:46.101 --> 00:09:47.634
Marry him, please.

160
00:09:47.636 --> 00:09:50.003
You're the only one
with any sense around here.

161
00:09:50.005 --> 00:09:52.238
With you wearing the pants,
there's still hope.

162
00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:53.574
- Wow!
- Gobber...

163
00:09:53.576 --> 00:09:56.377
Not awkward at all.

164
00:09:56.379 --> 00:09:58.244
Astrid, don't be like that.

165
00:09:58.246 --> 00:10:00.915
Whoa. That is a definitive no.

166
00:10:00.917 --> 00:10:03.349
Look, if you need
a beard to cry on,

167
00:10:03.351 --> 00:10:05.518
just lean on my shoulder
and you can cry into

168
00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.521
my full, thick beard.

169
00:10:07.523 --> 00:10:09.390
Oh, thank you, Tuffnut.

170
00:10:09.392 --> 00:10:11.090
Thank you.

171
00:10:11.092 --> 00:10:12.660
So much.

172
00:10:12.662 --> 00:10:14.661
Eret, son of Eret!

173
00:10:14.663 --> 00:10:17.263
What's the report?

174
00:10:17.265 --> 00:10:19.934
Two more trapper barges
spotted in the strait.

175
00:10:19.936 --> 00:10:21.669
So we go after them.

176
00:10:21.671 --> 00:10:23.704
- What?
- One day,

177
00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:27.074
you're gonna pick a fight
you can't win.

178
00:10:56.038 --> 00:10:57.738
Archers!

179
00:11:03.546 --> 00:11:06.412
- Dragon killers.
- Stay on your guard.

180
00:11:06.414 --> 00:11:08.350
Deathgrippers.

181
00:11:21.563 --> 00:11:24.297
Back! Do what I say, now!

182
00:11:24.299 --> 00:11:26.266
Do what I say!

183
00:11:26.268 --> 00:11:29.002
Grab the other head
on that Zippleback!

184
00:11:29.004 --> 00:11:30.337
You belong to the...

185
00:11:30.339 --> 00:11:33.107
The dragon riders
attacked us here,

186
00:11:33.109 --> 00:11:34.541
off the Eastern Strait.

187
00:11:36.578 --> 00:11:38.746
- Ragnar.
- Um, sorry.

188
00:11:38.748 --> 00:11:41.080
My dear warlords.

189
00:11:41.082 --> 00:11:45.185
How go your plans
to conquer the world?

190
00:11:46.788 --> 00:11:49.723
Grimmel, my old friend.

191
00:11:49.725 --> 00:11:51.057
Thank you for coming.

192
00:11:51.059 --> 00:11:53.026
Oh!

193
00:11:53.028 --> 00:11:55.661
A year since Drago's defeat,

194
00:11:55.663 --> 00:11:59.499
and no further along
with your dragon army, I see.

195
00:11:59.501 --> 00:12:02.136
You can thank the young chief
of Berk for that.

196
00:12:02.138 --> 00:12:03.804
Stoick's boy?

197
00:12:03.806 --> 00:12:07.373
Yep, he and his
peace-loving dragon riders

198
00:12:07.375 --> 00:12:11.277
continue to raid our ships
and steal our dragons.

199
00:12:11.279 --> 00:12:13.814
Mm. That does sound
like a nuisance.

200
00:12:13.816 --> 00:12:16.050
But I'm in the business
of killing dragons,

201
00:12:16.052 --> 00:12:18.051
not retrieving them.

202
00:12:18.053 --> 00:12:20.219
- But, Grimmel...
- That idiot boy has done

203
00:12:20.221 --> 00:12:21.655
all of the work for you,

204
00:12:21.657 --> 00:12:24.090
gathering the dragons
in one place.

205
00:12:24.092 --> 00:12:25.459
Why bother me?

206
00:12:25.461 --> 00:12:29.132
Because the flock is protected
by a Night Fury.

207
00:12:33.134 --> 00:12:34.634
Not possible.

208
00:12:34.636 --> 00:12:38.604
It seems one slipped
through your fingers.

209
00:12:38.606 --> 00:12:42.309
Look, Berk's dragons
will follow the alpha.

210
00:12:42.311 --> 00:12:47.647
So we'll pay you to capture him
and bring the flock to us.

211
00:12:47.649 --> 00:12:50.452
We even have
your favorite bait.

212
00:12:53.522 --> 00:12:56.790
The only dragon they left us
from last night's raid.

213
00:12:56.792 --> 00:13:00.326
A female? Hmm.

214
00:13:02.097 --> 00:13:05.799
So, do we have a deal,
old friend?

215
00:13:09.437 --> 00:13:10.572
Watch out!

216
00:13:19.648 --> 00:13:21.714
When all is said and done,

217
00:13:21.716 --> 00:13:25.384
this young chief will
bring me the Night Fury.

218
00:13:25.386 --> 00:13:31.093
They don't have a leader,
just a boy.

219
00:13:33.195 --> 00:13:35.496
Hiccup.

220
00:13:37.799 --> 00:13:41.167
This is Berk, son.

221
00:13:41.169 --> 00:13:43.337
It's our home.

222
00:13:43.339 --> 00:13:45.638
It was the home
of your grandparents

223
00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.374
and their grandparents
before them.

224
00:13:48.376 --> 00:13:52.378
And it's my job as chief
to protect us, Hiccup.

225
00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.680
And one day,
when you're all grown up,

226
00:13:54.682 --> 00:13:56.849
that job will be
passed on to you.

227
00:13:56.851 --> 00:13:58.584
Okay.

228
00:13:58.586 --> 00:14:01.921
And it's very important, son,
because out there,

229
00:14:01.923 --> 00:14:06.693
beyond the sunset,
lies the home of the dragons.

230
00:14:06.695 --> 00:14:09.662
- Wow.
- Aye.

231
00:14:09.664 --> 00:14:12.900
Legends tell of ships
that sailed too close to it,

232
00:14:12.902 --> 00:14:15.636
only to drop off
the edge of the world,

233
00:14:15.638 --> 00:14:18.504
never to be seen again.

234
00:14:18.506 --> 00:14:20.706
But those sailors
who turned back

235
00:14:20.708 --> 00:14:23.643
told tales of a great waterfall

236
00:14:23.645 --> 00:14:27.214
and dragons guarding
the entrance to a Hidden World.

237
00:14:27.216 --> 00:14:30.217
- Whoa.
- Not just a nest, Hiccup,

238
00:14:30.219 --> 00:14:33.686
but a land from which
all dragons come.

239
00:14:33.688 --> 00:14:36.522
Even Night Furies?

240
00:14:36.524 --> 00:14:38.324
Especially Night Furies.

241
00:14:38.326 --> 00:14:40.761
Those are scary.

242
00:14:40.763 --> 00:14:42.296
Don't you worry.

243
00:14:42.298 --> 00:14:45.232
One day, I'll find
the Hidden World

244
00:14:45.234 --> 00:14:47.401
and seal it up,

245
00:14:47.403 --> 00:14:51.341
so that people and dragons
will fight no more.

246
00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:03.217
What?

247
00:15:04.653 --> 00:15:06.386
Oh, all right.

248
00:15:06.388 --> 00:15:08.689
You do know it's not
a chew toy, don't you?

249
00:15:08.691 --> 00:15:10.958
Is this what you want?
Oh, do you want this leg?

250
00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:13.463
Do you want my leg?
Go get it.

251
00:15:25.006 --> 00:15:27.843
Getting pretty good
at gliding on your own, bud.

252
00:15:40.956 --> 00:15:44.757
Oh, so this is where you come
to get away from Gobber.

253
00:15:44.759 --> 00:15:47.563
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

254
00:15:49.331 --> 00:15:51.797
Ugh.

255
00:15:51.799 --> 00:15:53.499
Well, he's right, you know.

256
00:15:53.501 --> 00:15:55.368
R-Really?

257
00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.470
You think you and I should...?

258
00:15:57.472 --> 00:15:58.738
Oh, gods, no.

259
00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:00.741
We're nowhere near
ready for that.

260
00:16:00.743 --> 00:16:02.743
No, that's-that's crazy.

261
00:16:02.745 --> 00:16:05.545
I mean, he's right
about all of this.

262
00:16:05.547 --> 00:16:09.682
It does seem like the
whole world knows about us now.

263
00:16:09.684 --> 00:16:12.051
Yep. And the more dragons
we bring back here,

264
00:16:12.053 --> 00:16:14.454
the bigger of a target
we become.

265
00:16:14.456 --> 00:16:15.689
Ugh.

266
00:16:15.691 --> 00:16:19.925
I just wish there was some way
to make them leave us alone.

267
00:16:19.927 --> 00:16:21.496
There might be.

268
00:16:23.599 --> 00:16:26.932
Dad used to talk about
an old mariners' myth,

269
00:16:26.934 --> 00:16:29.469
of a secret land
at the edge of the world

270
00:16:29.471 --> 00:16:31.738
where dragons live
totally out of reach.

271
00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.742
Well, sailors are
known for tall tales.

272
00:16:35.744 --> 00:16:38.778
True. But what if it's real?

273
00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.815
It could be the answer
to all of our problems.

274
00:16:41.817 --> 00:16:45.352
How? By moving
the dragons there?

275
00:16:45.354 --> 00:16:48.088
Uh-uh. All of us.

276
00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:49.922
Seriously?

277
00:16:49.924 --> 00:16:53.493
And abandon our home
of seven generations?

278
00:16:53.495 --> 00:16:56.897
The home your father left you to protect.

279
00:16:56.899 --> 00:16:58.464
Uh...

280
00:16:58.466 --> 00:17:00.599
Yeah, I think we need
a real solution, Hiccup.

281
00:17:06.342 --> 00:17:08.342
Well, we could just
take Gobber's advice

282
00:17:08.344 --> 00:17:09.575
and tie the knot.

283
00:17:09.577 --> 00:17:11.577
That should fix everything.

284
00:17:11.579 --> 00:17:14.480
But, hey, if you're having
doubts about yours truly,

285
00:17:14.482 --> 00:17:16.850
I'm pretty sure Snotlout's available.

286
00:17:16.852 --> 00:17:19.052
He only has eyes for your mom.

287
00:17:21.423 --> 00:17:24.357
- Playing dirty now, huh?
- You asked for it.

288
00:17:24.359 --> 00:17:26.860
Looks like there might be
a wedding after all.

289
00:17:26.862 --> 00:17:30.029
Oh, how dare you? That is a low blow.

290
00:17:30.031 --> 00:17:32.732
No, no, you are not
getting away.

291
00:17:32.734 --> 00:17:34.968
Okay, okay, you win, you win!

292
00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.536
You always win.

293
00:17:37.538 --> 00:17:39.405
You knew what you were
getting into.

294
00:17:39.407 --> 00:17:41.743
Uh-huh. Right.

295
00:17:47.482 --> 00:17:48.917
Uh, bud?

296
00:17:52.653 --> 00:17:55.654
What... Yeah, sure,
don't bother to wait for us.

297
00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.135
Oh, my gods.

298
00:19:50.137 --> 00:19:51.872
Uh, Hiccup!

299
00:19:51.874 --> 00:19:53.809
Oh!

300
00:19:58.046 --> 00:20:00.613
Yeah, yeah, w-we're friends.
No need to kill us.

301
00:20:20.067 --> 00:20:22.635
- Wow.
- Another Night Fury.

302
00:20:22.637 --> 00:20:25.538
No, not quite.
It's more like a...

303
00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.307
- Bright... Fury.
- A Light Fury.

304
00:20:28.309 --> 00:20:31.010
Yeah, yours is better,
probably.

305
00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.314
<i>What do you mean, gone?</i>

306
00:20:34.316 --> 00:20:36.615
Vanished, into thin air.

307
00:20:36.617 --> 00:20:38.817
- What do you think?
- Uh-uh.

308
00:20:38.819 --> 00:20:40.687
Stubbier ears.
No dorsal plates.

309
00:20:40.689 --> 00:20:42.188
Okay. Got it.

310
00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:44.024
What a night.

311
00:20:44.026 --> 00:20:45.892
Bud, what's gotten into you?

312
00:20:45.894 --> 00:20:48.228
What is all this
slobbering and panting?

313
00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:52.599
Isn't it obvious?
He's in love.

314
00:20:52.601 --> 00:20:55.669
Trust me, relationships are
nothing but pain and misery.

315
00:20:57.005 --> 00:20:59.305
What did I just say?

316
00:20:59.307 --> 00:21:01.040
A-Am I not enough?

317
00:21:03.077 --> 00:21:04.978
I think that's a no.

318
00:21:16.791 --> 00:21:18.857
- Something like this?
- You know what?

319
00:21:18.859 --> 00:21:20.293
Just trace your Toothless card
and make her white.

320
00:21:20.295 --> 00:21:22.228
- You could've led with that.
- Can you believe it?

321
00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:24.229
Toothless has a girlfriend.

322
00:21:24.231 --> 00:21:26.266
I never took you
for a romantic.

323
00:21:26.268 --> 00:21:27.801
Like, ever.

324
00:21:27.803 --> 00:21:29.768
But it's so sweet.

325
00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:32.171
I mean, look.

326
00:21:39.914 --> 00:21:41.715
Okay. That's just sad.

327
00:21:41.717 --> 00:21:44.217
- And weird.
- Yeah, you better do something.

328
00:21:44.219 --> 00:21:47.821
Seriously? I'd rather shovel
poop all day than watch that.

329
00:21:47.823 --> 00:21:49.823
All right.
Let's head back to the woods

330
00:21:49.825 --> 00:21:51.259
and see if we can find her.

331
00:21:54.663 --> 00:21:55.929
Ah, good idea.

332
00:21:55.931 --> 00:21:57.263
A little privacy.

333
00:21:57.265 --> 00:21:58.998
- Uh...
- Shh.

334
00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.366
- It's boy talk.
- What?

335
00:22:00.368 --> 00:22:03.036
Come on,
let's go work this out.

336
00:22:03.038 --> 00:22:04.336
So, you want to get married.

337
00:22:04.338 --> 00:22:05.872
Uh, no, actually.

338
00:22:05.874 --> 00:22:07.774
Good news.
I've been to two weddings.

339
00:22:07.776 --> 00:22:11.644
I crashed both, but none
as high profile as this one.

340
00:22:11.646 --> 00:22:14.279
Lots of pressure, judgment,
and not just by me.

341
00:22:14.281 --> 00:22:16.815
Look, we talked about it.
We're not getting married.

342
00:22:16.817 --> 00:22:19.419
Cold feet.
I've seen it before.

343
00:22:19.421 --> 00:22:22.689
Don't worry, Little Hiccy.
I'm here.

344
00:22:22.691 --> 00:22:24.157
Wait, Hiccy?

345
00:22:24.159 --> 00:22:26.159
Now, I've seen the way
Astrid looks at you.

346
00:22:26.161 --> 00:22:27.693
Everyone has. That doubt.

347
00:22:27.695 --> 00:22:29.129
That not so subtle
disappointment.

348
00:22:29.131 --> 00:22:32.132
That longing for something
more than you.

349
00:22:32.134 --> 00:22:34.034
You need to focus on
being worthy.

350
00:22:34.036 --> 00:22:36.036
I mean, she's a warrior queen,
for Thor's sake.

351
00:22:36.038 --> 00:22:39.038
And you are neither.

352
00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:40.739
But with me as your best man...

353
00:22:40.741 --> 00:22:42.409
your spirit guide,
if you will...

354
00:22:42.411 --> 00:22:45.411
you'll learn to embrace
your inner Viking.

355
00:22:45.413 --> 00:22:47.413
Show these naysayers,
of which there are many,

356
00:22:47.415 --> 00:22:50.850
that you're more than
just a malnourished runt

357
00:22:50.852 --> 00:22:53.452
with bad hair, strange teeth,
and a twig for a neck.

358
00:22:53.454 --> 00:22:56.422
You're-you're
really bad at pep talks.

359
00:22:56.424 --> 00:22:58.391
Stop letting these insecurities

360
00:22:58.393 --> 00:22:59.992
get the best of you.

361
00:22:59.994 --> 00:23:02.161
Everyone's watching.
I mean, everyone.

362
00:23:02.163 --> 00:23:04.163
You need to man up.
Do as I do.

363
00:23:04.165 --> 00:23:07.267
It'll be hard,
but you have my word.

364
00:23:07.269 --> 00:23:10.437
And until I break that word,
I won't give up.

365
00:23:10.439 --> 00:23:12.337
Hey.

366
00:23:12.339 --> 00:23:15.141
Hey! What, am I wasting
my time here?

367
00:23:15.143 --> 00:23:18.814
You see some shiny thing in
the woods... Ooh, what is that?

368
00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:31.024
Toothless!

369
00:23:31.026 --> 00:23:32.758
Don't move a muscle.

370
00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:34.997
Hey!

371
00:23:43.739 --> 00:23:45.238
- Someone's here.
- Huh?

372
00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:46.905
He managed to slip
past our scouts

373
00:23:46.907 --> 00:23:48.373
and lay a trap in the woods.

374
00:23:48.375 --> 00:23:51.210
- It ruined boy talk.
- Oh.

375
00:23:51.212 --> 00:23:53.479
- Gah, let me at him!
- Slow down, Gobber.

376
00:23:53.481 --> 00:23:56.315
Let's get a search team on
the ground, scouts in the air.

377
00:23:56.317 --> 00:23:58.351
Toothless and I
will fly the coastline.

378
00:23:58.353 --> 00:24:02.322
Yeah, I wouldn't advise taking
Toothless anywhere, Chief.

379
00:24:02.324 --> 00:24:04.490
I know this handiwork.

380
00:24:04.492 --> 00:24:07.826
Grimmel the Grisly.
Famous back where I'm from.

381
00:24:07.828 --> 00:24:10.130
The smartest dragon hunter
I ever met.

382
00:24:10.132 --> 00:24:12.231
Well, next to me, of course.

383
00:24:12.233 --> 00:24:15.434
Well, he can't be that smart.
He left his trap unmanned.

384
00:24:15.436 --> 00:24:19.773
Nothing's accidental
when it comes to old Grimmel.

385
00:24:19.775 --> 00:24:21.440
He lives for the hunt,

386
00:24:21.442 --> 00:24:23.442
to get inside the mind
of his prey,

387
00:24:23.444 --> 00:24:25.911
to control its every choice.

388
00:24:25.913 --> 00:24:27.479
It's all a game to him.

389
00:24:27.481 --> 00:24:29.414
Well, he doesn't know
who he's playing with.

390
00:24:29.416 --> 00:24:31.417
Yeah. Well, we've dealt with
his kind before.

391
00:24:31.419 --> 00:24:33.452
Don't underestimate him,
Hiccup.

392
00:24:33.454 --> 00:24:36.189
Mark my words.
He'll be back.

393
00:24:36.191 --> 00:24:38.794
Then we'll be waiting for him.

394
00:24:52.073 --> 00:24:53.539
All right.

395
00:24:53.541 --> 00:24:55.941
All right, come on,
give me a clue here.

396
00:24:55.943 --> 00:24:58.114
Give me a clue, Dad.

397
00:25:19.067 --> 00:25:21.936
Oh, I hope you don't mind
if I help myself.

398
00:25:23.939 --> 00:25:25.875
This is, uh, mmm, quite good.

399
00:25:27.576 --> 00:25:30.980
Oh, that is impressive.
But let me finish my drink.

400
00:25:34.883 --> 00:25:35.883
Toothless!

401
00:25:38.987 --> 00:25:41.321
What did you do to him?

402
00:25:41.323 --> 00:25:44.257
Eh, nothing
that he won't sleep off.

403
00:25:47.494 --> 00:25:48.862
May I?

404
00:25:48.864 --> 00:25:49.997
Chief Hiccup.

405
00:25:49.999 --> 00:25:54.033
Hmm? Do I say Chief
or do I call you Hiccup?

406
00:25:54.035 --> 00:25:55.304
What do you prefer?

407
00:25:57.105 --> 00:26:02.007
You have no idea
who I am, do you?

408
00:26:02.009 --> 00:26:03.876
Oh.

409
00:26:03.878 --> 00:26:06.112
Well, your father knew of me.

410
00:26:06.114 --> 00:26:09.015
Now, there was a chief.

411
00:26:09.017 --> 00:26:13.620
One of the greatest dragon
hunters to have ever lived.

412
00:26:13.622 --> 00:26:16.189
What would he think of you?

413
00:26:19.627 --> 00:26:21.326
He had it right, you know.

414
00:26:21.328 --> 00:26:23.328
Making it his mission
to destroy the beasts

415
00:26:23.330 --> 00:26:25.597
so that you could grow up
in a better world.

416
00:26:25.599 --> 00:26:27.566
He changed his mind.

417
00:26:27.568 --> 00:26:29.938
And look where that got him.

418
00:26:31.439 --> 00:26:34.641
So let's get to the point.

419
00:26:34.643 --> 00:26:37.343
I am the Night Fury killer.

420
00:26:37.345 --> 00:26:41.914
I've hunted
every last one but yours.

421
00:26:41.916 --> 00:26:44.517
You are going to give me
that dragon, or I will...

422
00:26:44.519 --> 00:26:46.419
I will never give him up.

423
00:26:48.589 --> 00:26:53.428
You wish dragons to live free
among us like equals?

424
00:26:55.297 --> 00:26:57.497
A toxic notion, my boy.

425
00:26:57.499 --> 00:27:01.133
History has shown that we are
the superior species.

426
00:27:01.135 --> 00:27:05.604
What if word of your
misguided ideas were to spread?

427
00:27:05.606 --> 00:27:08.708
It would be the undoing
of civilization

428
00:27:08.710 --> 00:27:12.245
as we know it.

429
00:27:12.247 --> 00:27:14.182
Hmm.

430
00:27:18.019 --> 00:27:20.256
Did we get him?

431
00:27:22.423 --> 00:27:23.423
Now!

432
00:27:25.527 --> 00:27:27.093
Sorry to barge in.

433
00:27:27.095 --> 00:27:30.028
You think you can
come into my home,

434
00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:34.199
sit in my father's chair,
and threaten my dragon?

435
00:27:34.201 --> 00:27:36.169
This is Berk.

436
00:27:36.171 --> 00:27:39.671
And we have defended our way of
life from far worse than you.

437
00:27:39.673 --> 00:27:41.440
Ooh.

438
00:27:41.442 --> 00:27:44.376
A fighting spirit.
I love it.

439
00:27:44.378 --> 00:27:47.713
Only I'm afraid
you're mistaken.

440
00:27:47.715 --> 00:27:51.351
You've never seen
anything like me.

441
00:28:00.428 --> 00:28:01.630
Astrid, look out!

442
00:28:08.737 --> 00:28:10.737
Look out! Son, get clear.

443
00:28:13.074 --> 00:28:15.009
Run!

444
00:28:22.349 --> 00:28:24.650
Have my dragon ready

445
00:28:24.652 --> 00:28:29.658
when I return, or I will
destroy everything you love.

446
00:28:37.265 --> 00:28:41.100
- Grab the buckets!
- How did this happen?!

447
00:28:43.038 --> 00:28:45.037
- Inside.
- It's the middle of the night.

448
00:28:45.039 --> 00:28:47.305
- What are we doing here?
- All right.

449
00:28:47.307 --> 00:28:50.078
All right, everybody.
Settle down, please.

450
00:28:51.211 --> 00:28:53.112
Fishlegs.

451
00:28:53.114 --> 00:28:55.547
Have you ever seen
that species of dragon before?

452
00:28:58.420 --> 00:28:59.485
Let me at him!

453
00:28:59.487 --> 00:29:01.319
I'll give him
a piece of my mind!

454
00:29:01.321 --> 00:29:04.123
And by mind, I mean fist!

455
00:29:04.125 --> 00:29:06.625
Did you miss the part
where we almost died?

456
00:29:06.627 --> 00:29:09.261
Have you seen my house?

457
00:29:09.263 --> 00:29:11.730
This is a new kind of enemy.

458
00:29:11.732 --> 00:29:14.400
And I underestimated him.
Now, that's on me.

459
00:29:14.402 --> 00:29:16.401
But I will not do that again.

460
00:29:16.403 --> 00:29:19.639
We're Vikings.
We don't run from a fight.

461
00:29:19.641 --> 00:29:21.740
At least, I don't.
You might.

462
00:29:21.742 --> 00:29:23.609
I agree with Hiccup.

463
00:29:23.611 --> 00:29:25.611
We haven't seen
the last of Grimmel.

464
00:29:25.613 --> 00:29:28.514
He's a predator,
single-minded and patient.

465
00:29:28.516 --> 00:29:30.682
He won't stop
until he gets what he wants.

466
00:29:30.684 --> 00:29:31.784
I'm with Eret.

467
00:29:31.786 --> 00:29:34.786
We have to take
this threat seriously.

468
00:29:34.788 --> 00:29:36.788
Grimmel is just
a sign of the times.

469
00:29:36.790 --> 00:29:40.226
Our enemies are getting
smarter, more determined.

470
00:29:40.228 --> 00:29:44.663
We're not just overcrowded.
We are exposed and vulnerable.

471
00:29:44.665 --> 00:29:48.267
Short of full-blown war
and risking everyone we love,

472
00:29:48.269 --> 00:29:51.536
I don't...

473
00:29:51.538 --> 00:29:54.873
I don't see a way
of staying here any longer.

474
00:29:54.875 --> 00:29:56.642
What would Stoick think of this?

475
00:29:56.644 --> 00:29:59.213
Hey! Hear him out!

476
00:30:05.286 --> 00:30:08.621
If we want to live in peace
with our dragons,

477
00:30:08.623 --> 00:30:10.655
we need a better plan.

478
00:30:10.657 --> 00:30:13.359
So what are you saying, Chief?

479
00:30:13.361 --> 00:30:15.527
I'm saying
we have to disappear.

480
00:30:15.529 --> 00:30:17.462
Off the map.

481
00:30:17.464 --> 00:30:20.699
Take the dragons to a place
where no one will find them.

482
00:30:20.701 --> 00:30:22.701
And where might that be?

483
00:30:22.703 --> 00:30:25.537
He's talking about a quest
for the Hidden World.

484
00:30:25.539 --> 00:30:26.405
The hidden what?

485
00:30:26.407 --> 00:30:28.540
- Out to lunch.
- Yeah.

486
00:30:28.542 --> 00:30:31.544
My father was obsessed with it
when I was a boy.

487
00:30:31.546 --> 00:30:33.312
He made notes and maps

488
00:30:33.314 --> 00:30:37.150
in search of the ancestral home
of all dragons,

489
00:30:37.152 --> 00:30:40.385
tucked away somewhere
beyond the edge of the world.

490
00:30:40.387 --> 00:30:42.521
It may be the solution we need.

491
00:30:42.523 --> 00:30:45.357
We are dragon people.

492
00:30:45.359 --> 00:30:47.459
It's where we belong.

493
00:30:47.461 --> 00:30:51.463
Look, I know this is our home.

494
00:30:51.465 --> 00:30:54.232
My father left me
to protect it.

495
00:30:54.234 --> 00:30:57.236
But Berk is more
than this place.

496
00:30:57.238 --> 00:30:59.171
We are Berk.

497
00:30:59.173 --> 00:31:00.805
The people, the dragons.

498
00:31:00.807 --> 00:31:04.576
I say Berk is wherever we go.

499
00:31:04.578 --> 00:31:05.911
I don't know.

500
00:31:05.913 --> 00:31:07.279
What do you think?

501
00:31:07.281 --> 00:31:10.283
I'm with him! Who else?!

502
00:31:29.369 --> 00:31:30.769
Excuse me. Coming through.

503
00:31:30.771 --> 00:31:32.872
Just, let me just
get right through here.

504
00:31:32.874 --> 00:31:36.709
Fishmeat, look, eat your rocks.
Eat your rocks.

505
00:31:36.711 --> 00:31:39.211
Gods! People who fly
with babies are the worst.

506
00:31:41.382 --> 00:31:43.949
I feel like I'm always asking
you this question, but...

507
00:31:43.951 --> 00:31:45.951
Wake up, Grump! Wake up!

508
00:31:45.953 --> 00:31:48.353
Is there an actual plan or...?

509
00:31:48.355 --> 00:31:51.457
Just keep flying until
we reach the end of the world.

510
00:31:51.459 --> 00:31:53.926
Ah. Seems sensible.

511
00:31:53.928 --> 00:31:56.728
<i>So, where are they?</i>

512
00:31:56.730 --> 00:31:58.663
Gone. Obviously.

513
00:31:58.665 --> 00:32:00.799
The Night Fury escaped you?

514
00:32:00.801 --> 00:32:02.969
- Again?
- I encouraged it.

515
00:32:02.971 --> 00:32:06.404
They've abandoned
their only defensible position.

516
00:32:06.406 --> 00:32:08.007
<i>Running scared</i>

517
00:32:08.009 --> 00:32:10.409
<i>with what little
they can carry.</i>

518
00:32:10.411 --> 00:32:12.311
It just keeps going.

519
00:32:12.313 --> 00:32:15.014
That's 'cause the world
is actually round.

520
00:32:15.016 --> 00:32:16.615
The sun's round. The moon is round.

521
00:32:16.617 --> 00:32:17.984
Stars are round.

522
00:32:17.986 --> 00:32:19.818
Even though
they're small and stupid.

523
00:32:19.820 --> 00:32:22.854
Right? Stars.

524
00:32:22.856 --> 00:32:25.024
Don't fret.
They won't get far.

525
00:32:25.026 --> 00:32:28.294
The Night Fury is distracted.

526
00:32:28.296 --> 00:32:31.998
I introduced him
to your female.

527
00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:33.999
<i>Furies mate for life, you see.</i>

528
00:32:34.001 --> 00:32:36.869
What you picking up on, bud?

529
00:32:38.972 --> 00:32:40.472
The Light Fury!

530
00:32:40.474 --> 00:32:41.873
- She's following us!
- Wow!

531
00:32:41.875 --> 00:32:43.875
Cool.

532
00:32:45.913 --> 00:32:47.912
- Would ya look at that?
- Where'd she go?

533
00:32:47.914 --> 00:32:49.882
Is she made of sky?

534
00:32:49.884 --> 00:32:52.221
Whoa! Hold up, Toothless!

535
00:32:58.625 --> 00:33:01.026
Well, look who it is.

536
00:33:01.028 --> 00:33:03.728
Uh...

537
00:33:03.730 --> 00:33:05.363
Oh, hey, it's really nice
to finally...

538
00:33:16.844 --> 00:33:20.046
This is perfect. So great.

539
00:33:20.048 --> 00:33:21.883
Not a word.

540
00:33:24.719 --> 00:33:26.686
<i>Y-Yes, yes,
but where did they go?</i>

541
00:33:26.688 --> 00:33:29.322
I have to explain this.

542
00:33:29.324 --> 00:33:31.990
Night Furies can't survive
in the cold,

543
00:33:31.992 --> 00:33:33.226
so they haven't gone north.

544
00:33:33.228 --> 00:33:35.327
<i>They're trying to put distance
between themselves</i>

545
00:33:35.329 --> 00:33:36.696
<i>and enemies to the east</i>

546
00:33:36.698 --> 00:33:38.029
and south.

547
00:33:38.031 --> 00:33:39.864
<i>And Night Furies cannot fly</i>

548
00:33:39.866 --> 00:33:43.602
<i>long distances without rest.</i>

549
00:33:43.604 --> 00:33:46.072
Their flight path
must include stops.

550
00:33:46.074 --> 00:33:47.476
Potty break!

551
00:33:49.376 --> 00:33:52.111
<i>Therefore, they've gone...</i>

552
00:33:54.115 --> 00:33:56.884
<i>They can only have gone...</i>

553
00:33:58.952 --> 00:34:02.421
<i>Does anyone want
to take a guess?</i>

554
00:34:02.423 --> 00:34:03.855
Anyone?

555
00:34:03.857 --> 00:34:05.857
W-W... W-W-W...

556
00:34:05.859 --> 00:34:07.992
Ah, east!

557
00:34:07.994 --> 00:34:09.729
West.

558
00:34:09.731 --> 00:34:12.565
Hmm? Simple, you see?

559
00:34:12.567 --> 00:34:14.566
Oh, isn't this fun?

560
00:34:14.568 --> 00:34:16.735
Yes? No?

561
00:34:18.405 --> 00:34:20.706
Yes. Yes.

562
00:34:20.708 --> 00:34:23.041
Where is your love of the hunt?

563
00:34:23.043 --> 00:34:25.577
I thought you were conquerors.

564
00:34:25.579 --> 00:34:27.780
You'll have your prize in time.

565
00:34:27.782 --> 00:34:32.751
Just allow me a few more days
to enjoy this.

566
00:34:32.753 --> 00:34:34.753
I have dearly missed it.

567
00:34:34.755 --> 00:34:36.389
<i>All right.</i>

568
00:34:36.391 --> 00:34:38.557
Looks like we're camping here
for tonight.

569
00:34:38.559 --> 00:34:40.525
Well, thank Thor for that.

570
00:34:40.527 --> 00:34:42.528
Yes. My own place.

571
00:34:42.530 --> 00:34:45.898
I plan to build a hut,
only for the bearded.

572
00:34:45.900 --> 00:34:47.766
Ruffnut, you got to stay out.

573
00:34:47.768 --> 00:34:49.568
Chin whiskers don't count.

574
00:34:49.570 --> 00:34:52.771
I see a tower of
manliness in the shape of me.

575
00:34:52.773 --> 00:34:56.008
It's gonna be taller than Eret
with bigger muscles.

576
00:34:56.010 --> 00:34:57.543
W-What?

577
00:34:57.545 --> 00:34:59.644
- Get out of my house!
- Hey.

578
00:34:59.646 --> 00:35:01.679
- Is there a problem here?
- Yeah, there's a problem.

579
00:35:01.681 --> 00:35:02.981
Ever since you showed up,

580
00:35:02.983 --> 00:35:04.550
you've been trying
to upstage me.

581
00:35:04.552 --> 00:35:06.751
You're just so jealous.
It's delusional.

582
00:35:06.753 --> 00:35:08.653
Yeah, delusion's
a good word for it.

583
00:35:08.655 --> 00:35:10.188
Listen, son of Eret.

584
00:35:10.190 --> 00:35:12.624
When Hiccup blows it as chief,
I'm next in line.

585
00:35:12.626 --> 00:35:15.026
Number two, 'cause
I'm clearly Valka's favorite.

586
00:35:15.028 --> 00:35:17.963
So, you better start
showing me some respect.

587
00:35:19.132 --> 00:35:20.666
Strange little man.

588
00:35:20.668 --> 00:35:22.434
Ah, don't mind him.

589
00:35:22.436 --> 00:35:25.771
It's not your fault you have
the body of a Norse god.

590
00:35:25.773 --> 00:35:27.807
I myself have the same problem.

591
00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:30.943
This one's mine.

592
00:35:30.945 --> 00:35:33.646
Blacksmith's stall
goes right here.

593
00:35:34.648 --> 00:35:37.016
One, two, three, four, five.

594
00:35:37.018 --> 00:35:39.651
- Where's...? Oh.
- Uh, okay.

595
00:35:39.653 --> 00:35:42.054
Uh, hold on, gang.
I-I said make camp.

596
00:35:42.056 --> 00:35:45.124
- Did you see them?
- Not build a new village.

597
00:35:45.126 --> 00:35:47.025
Who died and made you chief?

598
00:35:47.027 --> 00:35:49.695
What? Ow!

599
00:35:49.697 --> 00:35:52.030
Granted, this place
is very nice,

600
00:35:52.032 --> 00:35:54.200
but it's not the Hidden World.

601
00:35:54.202 --> 00:35:57.202
We don't even know
if this Hidden World exists.

602
00:35:57.204 --> 00:36:00.472
Yeah. This place is real.

603
00:36:00.474 --> 00:36:02.240
Eh, there's nothing
more stubborn

604
00:36:02.242 --> 00:36:04.844
than a mob of
tired, hungry Vikings.

605
00:36:04.846 --> 00:36:08.914
Well, I guess this can
work as a base in the meantime.

606
00:36:08.916 --> 00:36:11.950
It's defensible, hidden.

607
00:36:11.952 --> 00:36:14.220
All right. You can stay.

608
00:36:14.222 --> 00:36:15.954
Say hello to New Berk!

609
00:36:15.956 --> 00:36:17.822
Let's get building, lads.

610
00:36:17.824 --> 00:36:20.226
Until Toothless and I
find the Hidden World.

611
00:36:20.228 --> 00:36:22.760
Get off it!

612
00:36:22.762 --> 00:36:24.229
Now, about that voice.

613
00:36:24.231 --> 00:36:27.700
Can we lose the whole
honking goose thing?

614
00:36:27.702 --> 00:36:29.934
It's hard to imagine
wedded bliss

615
00:36:29.936 --> 00:36:32.871
with that going off
every minute.

616
00:36:32.873 --> 00:36:34.740
If you're going
to continue west,

617
00:36:34.742 --> 00:36:37.041
I should head back to make sure
we weren't followed.

618
00:36:37.043 --> 00:36:39.278
Great idea. I'll go with you
for protection.

619
00:36:39.280 --> 00:36:42.914
No! You're far
too important here.

620
00:36:42.916 --> 00:36:45.184
Yeah.

621
00:36:45.186 --> 00:36:47.151
Just be careful.

622
00:36:47.153 --> 00:36:48.653
Look at this place!
It's amazing!

623
00:36:48.655 --> 00:36:50.555
- That's a nice rock.
- What?

624
00:36:50.557 --> 00:36:54.827
This plan to hide us
from the rest of the world.

625
00:36:54.829 --> 00:36:56.729
Though-though I wish
it were possible,

626
00:36:56.731 --> 00:36:59.264
I fear it can't last, Hiccup.

627
00:36:59.266 --> 00:37:03.034
I mean, you know I tried
to do the same for years.

628
00:37:03.036 --> 00:37:08.139
But greedy humans
always find a way.

629
00:37:08.141 --> 00:37:11.744
I just... I only ask
that you think about it.

630
00:37:11.746 --> 00:37:13.077
This one's mine.

631
00:37:13.079 --> 00:37:15.046
I threw my axe down first.

632
00:37:15.048 --> 00:37:17.682
Do you still think
I'm crazy or...?

633
00:37:17.684 --> 00:37:22.086
Let's just say
this whole idea is very you.

634
00:37:22.088 --> 00:37:24.255
Well, thanks for
supporting me last night.

635
00:37:24.257 --> 00:37:25.791
It meant a lot.

636
00:37:25.793 --> 00:37:28.327
Don't thank me yet.

637
00:37:28.329 --> 00:37:30.295
I just hope
you're right about this.

638
00:37:30.297 --> 00:37:33.767
- I like it here.
- I always wanted a sunset view.

639
00:37:50.650 --> 00:37:53.284
Toothless.
No, it's too early.

640
00:43:22.483 --> 00:43:24.552
Oh, now you can draw.

641
00:44:45.599 --> 00:44:47.632
- Oh. Someone hasn't slept.
- Yeah.

642
00:44:47.634 --> 00:44:51.103
Well, that Light Fury won't
let me within a mile of her.

643
00:44:51.105 --> 00:44:53.104
And neither of us
will be getting any sleep

644
00:44:53.106 --> 00:44:55.740
or finding the Hidden World
until Toothless takes over.

645
00:44:55.742 --> 00:44:57.409
Hey!

646
00:44:57.411 --> 00:44:59.577
What do you think of that?

647
00:44:59.579 --> 00:45:01.512
Yeah.

648
00:45:01.514 --> 00:45:03.682
You tried this once before.
He didn't want it.

649
00:45:03.684 --> 00:45:07.151
Well, until now,
he didn't have a reason to.

650
00:45:07.153 --> 00:45:08.588
Right, bud?

651
00:45:15.628 --> 00:45:17.628
What?

652
00:45:17.630 --> 00:45:20.599
No, nothing.
I'm-I'm impressed.

653
00:45:20.601 --> 00:45:23.501
I mean, look at you.
Embracing change.

654
00:45:23.503 --> 00:45:25.503
I am proud of you.

655
00:45:25.505 --> 00:45:27.505
Well, he's my best bud.

656
00:45:27.507 --> 00:45:29.508
I want him to be happy.

657
00:45:29.510 --> 00:45:32.080
Eh, besides, it's just
until he brings her back.

658
00:45:35.815 --> 00:45:38.617
All right.

659
00:45:38.619 --> 00:45:40.355
- Fire when ready.
- Oh!

660
00:45:46.226 --> 00:45:49.494
Well, I guess you know
the tail is fireproof.

661
00:45:49.496 --> 00:45:52.229
Okay, Toothless.

662
00:45:52.231 --> 00:45:54.066
Okay, okay. Okay, yes, I know.

663
00:45:54.068 --> 00:45:55.566
I know.

664
00:45:55.568 --> 00:45:58.070
Okay, I know.

665
00:45:58.072 --> 00:46:00.405
- Please, this is not helping.
- Well, well, well.

666
00:46:00.407 --> 00:46:02.173
Someone's excited.

667
00:46:02.175 --> 00:46:04.575
He's fresh off
his first date.

668
00:46:04.577 --> 00:46:06.545
Now he's love crazed.

669
00:46:06.547 --> 00:46:08.813
Only we're the ones
going crazy.

670
00:46:08.815 --> 00:46:12.117
The sooner he brings back
that Light Fury, the better.

671
00:46:12.119 --> 00:46:14.385
Yeah, but to do that,
he'll need to fly without me.

672
00:46:14.387 --> 00:46:17.255
So time to give this
new and improved baby a shot.

673
00:46:19.159 --> 00:46:22.726
Attaboy.
Looking sharp, Toothless!

674
00:46:22.728 --> 00:46:25.296
So what do you think, bud?

675
00:46:25.298 --> 00:46:26.697
Bring her home.

676
00:46:26.699 --> 00:46:29.867
By sundown at the latest.

677
00:46:29.869 --> 00:46:32.369
No, save it
for your girlfriend.

678
00:46:32.371 --> 00:46:34.207
Go on. Get out of here.

679
00:46:41.347 --> 00:46:43.481
It's okay.

680
00:47:41.440 --> 00:47:42.776
Watch out!

681
00:47:46.380 --> 00:47:48.679
Go, Cloudjumper!

682
00:51:00.639 --> 00:51:02.539
To the chief!

683
00:51:02.541 --> 00:51:03.842
To the chief!

684
00:51:03.844 --> 00:51:06.110
Aye. To our chief.

685
00:51:06.112 --> 00:51:08.146
Oh, a chip off the old block.

686
00:51:08.148 --> 00:51:11.115
Yeah, okay, guys.
Now I'm just getting sick.

687
00:51:11.117 --> 00:51:12.883
Okay.

688
00:51:12.885 --> 00:51:14.786
Got to say,

689
00:51:14.788 --> 00:51:16.621
I thought you were
well off your rocker,

690
00:51:16.623 --> 00:51:18.789
but this spot ain't half bad.

691
00:51:18.791 --> 00:51:21.659
This was supposed to be
a temporary solution.

692
00:51:21.661 --> 00:51:22.626
It's unanimous.

693
00:51:22.628 --> 00:51:25.396
Everyone agrees
we've definitely traded up.

694
00:51:25.398 --> 00:51:27.766
Well done, Chief.

695
00:51:27.768 --> 00:51:29.434
What if the tail broke?

696
00:51:29.436 --> 00:51:31.034
What if Grimmel found him?

697
00:51:31.036 --> 00:51:33.637
- What if he needs me?
- Would you relax?

698
00:51:33.639 --> 00:51:35.807
He's probably having
the time of his life.

699
00:51:35.809 --> 00:51:38.041
How would I know?
She never comes around.

700
00:51:38.043 --> 00:51:40.512
And when she does,
she's always rushing off.

701
00:51:40.514 --> 00:51:42.947
I'm saying how-how do we know

702
00:51:42.949 --> 00:51:44.615
if she's right for us?

703
00:51:44.617 --> 00:51:46.617
- Us?
- You know what I mean.

704
00:51:46.619 --> 00:51:49.487
She's so wild and skittish.
I'm just gonna say it.

705
00:51:49.489 --> 00:51:50.655
I don't trust her.

706
00:51:50.657 --> 00:51:53.458
Can't tame 'em all, Hiccup.

707
00:51:53.460 --> 00:51:55.959
One day, you'll have to snip
those apron strings

708
00:51:55.961 --> 00:51:58.128
and let Toothless
stretch his wings.

709
00:51:58.130 --> 00:52:01.199
Reminds me of a talk I had
with Stoick about you.

710
00:52:03.503 --> 00:52:05.436
Where do they keep coming from?

711
00:52:05.438 --> 00:52:08.005
- Who?
- Those bloody Hobgobblers.

712
00:52:08.007 --> 00:52:10.641
I swear they're popping up
faster than rabbits.

713
00:52:10.643 --> 00:52:12.644
I think they want to eat me.

714
00:52:12.646 --> 00:52:14.845
Evidence would suggest
I'm tasty.

715
00:52:14.847 --> 00:52:16.514
Hiccy, a moment?

716
00:52:16.516 --> 00:52:19.516
Listen, I've been
watching you walk.

717
00:52:19.518 --> 00:52:21.586
Lose the limp.
No one's gonna marry that.

718
00:52:21.588 --> 00:52:23.454
I have a prosthetic leg.

719
00:52:23.456 --> 00:52:25.623
- So have I.
- And I have a parasitic twin,

720
00:52:25.625 --> 00:52:28.025
but you don't see me
limping around about it.

721
00:52:28.027 --> 00:52:31.028
Come on. Chin up, Hiccy.
Puff out that chest.

722
00:52:31.030 --> 00:52:33.630
Move that butt to the left a little bit.

723
00:52:41.807 --> 00:52:44.575
Mom, are you hurt?
W-What happened out there?

724
00:52:44.577 --> 00:52:46.845
I don't know how,
but Grimmel is tracking us.

725
00:52:46.847 --> 00:52:50.715
Ah! This is all because
of the Hobgobblers.

726
00:52:50.717 --> 00:52:52.816
He has a hundred ships,
maybe more,

727
00:52:52.818 --> 00:52:55.820
with enough cages
for all of our dragons.

728
00:52:57.157 --> 00:52:58.856
If Grimmel is
leading them here,

729
00:52:58.858 --> 00:53:00.925
we have to take him
out of the mix.

730
00:53:00.927 --> 00:53:03.760
Uh, and how would we do that?

731
00:53:03.762 --> 00:53:05.762
By going there to capture him.

732
00:53:05.764 --> 00:53:07.932
Capture him?

733
00:53:07.934 --> 00:53:09.870
I'm with him! Who else?!

734
00:53:56.550 --> 00:54:00.251
Okay, split up.
We'll be harder to catch.

735
00:54:00.253 --> 00:54:02.820
I was thinking we should
split up, just because.

736
00:54:02.822 --> 00:54:05.055
I like your instincts.

737
00:54:05.057 --> 00:54:06.791
What is this?

738
00:54:45.898 --> 00:54:48.766
Shh! Shh! Quiet.

739
00:54:48.768 --> 00:54:50.334
- Quiet.
- Where's your dragon

740
00:54:50.336 --> 00:54:53.271
when you need him, hmm, Chief?

741
00:54:53.273 --> 00:54:56.874
Must have forgotten
all about you.

742
00:54:56.876 --> 00:54:58.943
First rule of the hunt:

743
00:54:58.945 --> 00:55:01.378
separate the prey
from its pack.

744
00:55:01.380 --> 00:55:05.383
You've just removed yourselves
from the equation.

745
00:55:05.385 --> 00:55:07.284
- Why are you doing this?
- Really?

746
00:55:07.286 --> 00:55:10.088
I didn't think you cared.

747
00:55:10.090 --> 00:55:12.856
Well, unlike you,
when I was a boy

748
00:55:12.858 --> 00:55:16.927
and I came upon a Night Fury,
I killed it where it slept.

749
00:55:16.929 --> 00:55:21.365
That simple act of courage
made me a hero in my village.

750
00:55:21.367 --> 00:55:24.901
So I decided
to kill every last one,

751
00:55:24.903 --> 00:55:28.373
bringing real peace
to the people of this world.

752
00:55:28.375 --> 00:55:30.374
Until you came along,

753
00:55:30.376 --> 00:55:33.644
preaching that dragons
are something other than

754
00:55:33.646 --> 00:55:35.813
thieves and murderers.

755
00:55:37.150 --> 00:55:40.684
That nonsense dies now,
starting with you.

756
00:55:40.686 --> 00:55:42.987
But you have dragons of your own.

757
00:55:42.989 --> 00:55:45.088
These?

758
00:55:45.090 --> 00:55:47.090
They're dragon killers,

759
00:55:47.092 --> 00:55:50.360
drugged into obedience
with their own venom.

760
00:55:50.362 --> 00:55:53.697
Not even your precious alpha
could control them.

761
00:55:53.699 --> 00:55:57.034
They serve me and only me.

762
00:55:57.036 --> 00:55:59.403
Allow me to demonstrate.

763
00:55:59.405 --> 00:56:01.204
Take cover!

764
00:56:05.378 --> 00:56:07.177
Split up!

765
00:56:07.179 --> 00:56:08.615
Whoa!

766
00:56:13.786 --> 00:56:15.722
Whoa! Run!

767
00:56:33.706 --> 00:56:35.308
Up here!

768
00:56:51.157 --> 00:56:53.093
Hurry!

769
00:56:55.027 --> 00:56:56.994
Go, go, go, go, go!

770
00:56:58.998 --> 00:57:00.266
Hiccup!

771
00:57:05.505 --> 00:57:07.170
Gotcha.

772
00:57:07.172 --> 00:57:08.840
Go, Cloudjumper!

773
00:57:14.146 --> 00:57:16.146
Yeah!

774
00:57:16.148 --> 00:57:18.085
Our hero!

775
00:57:29.896 --> 00:57:31.262
Hmm.

776
00:57:31.264 --> 00:57:34.034
Ugh, he takes
that stupid baby everywhere.

777
00:57:39.371 --> 00:57:41.072
God almighty!

778
00:57:41.074 --> 00:57:43.007
Guess we won't be
needing this then, huh?

779
00:57:43.009 --> 00:57:45.275
I led us right into his trap.

780
00:57:45.277 --> 00:57:48.479
Yeah, nice work, Chief.
Right, Ruff?

781
00:57:48.481 --> 00:57:50.014
Wait.

782
00:57:50.016 --> 00:57:51.481
- Uh...
- Where is Ruffnut?

783
00:57:51.483 --> 00:57:53.351
We-we left her behind?

784
00:57:53.353 --> 00:57:55.385
How could you not notice
she was missing?

785
00:57:55.387 --> 00:57:57.220
You ride a two-headed dragon.

786
00:57:57.222 --> 00:57:58.389
Oh, yeah.

787
00:57:58.391 --> 00:58:01.492
I feel like how Ruffnut is
every day: dumb.

788
00:58:01.494 --> 00:58:03.327
Odin be spanked!

789
00:58:03.329 --> 00:58:05.429
This just gets
better and better.

790
00:58:05.431 --> 00:58:06.963
Any more fantastic news?

791
00:58:06.965 --> 00:58:08.298
I try to avoid looking at her.

792
00:58:08.300 --> 00:58:09.833
It gives me acid reflux.

793
00:58:09.835 --> 00:58:12.036
O-Okay, guys,
just keep your helmets on.

794
00:58:12.038 --> 00:58:13.503
Toothless and I will find her.

795
00:58:13.505 --> 00:58:15.438
Toothless has
the Light Fury now.

796
00:58:15.440 --> 00:58:17.208
He's probably
not even coming back.

797
00:58:17.210 --> 00:58:18.441
What?

798
00:58:18.443 --> 00:58:20.443
You gave him
his freedom, Hiccup.

799
00:58:20.445 --> 00:58:22.345
What were you expecting?

800
00:58:22.347 --> 00:58:24.215
I never thought
he'd stay away for good!

801
00:58:24.217 --> 00:58:26.950
I-I...

802
00:58:26.952 --> 00:58:30.356
Look, I'll-I'll figure it out.
I just need more time.

803
00:58:31.958 --> 00:58:34.891
He thinks he has to lead alone.

804
00:58:34.893 --> 00:58:38.429
Well, because
his father had to.

805
00:58:38.431 --> 00:58:42.032
He doesn't realize
the strength you have together.

806
00:58:42.034 --> 00:58:45.436
- Do you still believe in him?
- Of course.

807
00:58:45.438 --> 00:58:47.237
I wish he did.

808
00:58:47.239 --> 00:58:51.608
But he thinks he's nothing
without Toothless.

809
00:58:51.610 --> 00:58:54.280
Then help him
realize the truth.

810
00:58:58.918 --> 00:59:00.083
- Get on.
- What?

811
00:59:00.085 --> 00:59:01.318
We're going to find him.

812
00:59:01.320 --> 00:59:03.554
Really?

813
00:59:03.556 --> 00:59:06.858
Everybody, stay put.

814
00:59:06.860 --> 00:59:09.559
We will get Ruffnut back.
Don't worry.

815
00:59:09.561 --> 00:59:11.229
Worry?

816
00:59:11.231 --> 00:59:14.030
If they're stuck with Ruffnut,
I'm more worried about them.

817
00:59:15.934 --> 00:59:19.436
Why the long face?

818
00:59:19.438 --> 00:59:21.505
I mean, mine's long,
but yours is really long.

819
00:59:21.507 --> 00:59:24.275
All face and no brain, like
you got stretched at birth.

820
00:59:24.277 --> 00:59:25.876
Do you have a twin, too?

821
00:59:25.878 --> 00:59:27.612
Tuffnut took up all the room
in Mom's belly.

822
00:59:27.614 --> 00:59:29.479
Otherwise I'd have
a rounder head and more brains.

823
00:59:29.481 --> 00:59:31.615
That's science.

824
00:59:31.617 --> 00:59:34.017
My braids are like
little Zipplebacks. See?

825
00:59:36.021 --> 00:59:38.389
Even the mold spots
look like eyes. It's so cute.

826
00:59:38.391 --> 00:59:40.090
They even have
little horns and everything,

827
00:59:40.092 --> 00:59:41.425
just like Barf and Belch.

828
00:59:41.427 --> 00:59:43.126
Except me and Barf
can't stand Belch,

829
00:59:43.128 --> 00:59:44.327
so they're really just Barfs.

830
00:59:44.329 --> 00:59:45.396
It's warm in here.

831
00:59:45.398 --> 00:59:47.565
I know what you're thinking.

832
00:59:47.567 --> 00:59:50.367
You've never had
a prisoner this hot.

833
00:59:50.369 --> 00:59:52.168
All the boys love me.

834
00:59:52.170 --> 00:59:54.304
Except Eret,
who totally lost his chance.

835
00:59:54.306 --> 00:59:56.340
That ship has sailed, boy.
Sorry.

836
00:59:56.342 --> 00:59:57.675
And Hiccup is
practically married

837
00:59:57.677 --> 00:59:58.842
to that round-head, Astrid.

838
00:59:58.844 --> 01:00:02.213
But Snotlout and Fishlegs,
they're basically my harem.

839
01:00:02.215 --> 01:00:04.615
I just can't choose, you know?

840
01:00:04.617 --> 01:00:07.217
Snotlout's a beefcake but
almost too pretty, you know?

841
01:00:07.219 --> 01:00:09.552
Sometimes I think he's more
in love with himself than me.

842
01:00:09.554 --> 01:00:12.923
There's only room for one
beauty in this relationship.

843
01:00:12.925 --> 01:00:15.492
Fishlegs would keep
me alive longer if I had to

844
01:00:15.494 --> 01:00:17.327
eat one of them, stranded
on some glacier somewhere.

845
01:00:17.329 --> 01:00:19.130
But he never shuts up about dragons.

846
01:00:19.132 --> 01:00:20.530
Don't you hate
when people never stop talking?

847
01:00:20.532 --> 01:00:22.432
- Yes, I do.
- They just keep going and going.

848
01:00:22.434 --> 01:00:24.936
Blah, blah, blah.
It's so boring.

849
01:00:24.938 --> 01:00:26.938
- Can't we just feed her to your dragons?
- I'm hungry.

850
01:00:26.940 --> 01:00:28.338
Hey, what do you have
to eat around here?

851
01:00:28.340 --> 01:00:29.606
I'm allergic to fish.
You should know that.

852
01:00:29.608 --> 01:00:32.943
That's all they have
at that stupid new island.

853
01:00:32.945 --> 01:00:34.512
Do you have any clams?

854
01:00:34.514 --> 01:00:36.347
They're like little mouths
with slimy food inside

855
01:00:36.349 --> 01:00:38.449
that's already chewed,
like the way Mom used to do it.

856
01:00:38.451 --> 01:00:41.619
Enough!

857
01:00:41.621 --> 01:00:44.054
Until I turned 12 and she was
like, "Chew your own food."

858
01:00:44.056 --> 01:00:45.623
And I was like,
"No, I kinda like it."

859
01:00:45.625 --> 01:00:48.358
Most annoying creature
ever to cross my path.

860
01:00:48.360 --> 01:00:50.161
Aw.

861
01:00:50.163 --> 01:00:53.264
Oops, you let the dragons out.

862
01:00:53.266 --> 01:00:55.132
I'm gonna get you.
I'm gonna get you.

863
01:00:55.134 --> 01:00:56.967
- No, this one's gonna get you.
- Get...

864
01:00:56.969 --> 01:00:59.302
Take him and go!

865
01:00:59.304 --> 01:01:02.039
Please! I beg you!

866
01:01:02.041 --> 01:01:04.441
The Deathgrippers
will have to forgo dinner.

867
01:01:04.443 --> 01:01:07.711
Ew, you feed
your dragons dragons?

868
01:01:07.713 --> 01:01:10.014
- Go!
- Where's your bathroom?

869
01:01:10.016 --> 01:01:11.115
I got to...

870
01:01:11.117 --> 01:01:13.416
Okay! Gods.

871
01:01:13.418 --> 01:01:16.487
No wonder you have gray hair.

872
01:01:16.489 --> 01:01:18.356
Stress is not good for you.

873
01:01:20.226 --> 01:01:22.162
So long, losers!

874
01:01:32.070 --> 01:01:34.704
- Where-where is she heading?
- She's tracking something.

875
01:01:34.706 --> 01:01:36.639
Aren't you, girl?

876
01:01:36.641 --> 01:01:39.642
There's nothing but
miles and miles of...

877
01:02:11.177 --> 01:02:13.309
A great waterfall.

878
01:02:13.311 --> 01:02:15.746
At the end of the world.

879
01:02:17.617 --> 01:02:19.553
Stormfly!

880
01:03:15.307 --> 01:03:17.307
Wow.

881
01:03:17.309 --> 01:03:19.246
Look.

882
01:03:53.512 --> 01:03:55.614
- Wow.
- Wow.

883
01:04:35.454 --> 01:04:37.954
It really does exist.

884
01:04:55.373 --> 01:04:58.208
- Toothless.
- Shh. You'll spook them.

885
01:05:40.552 --> 01:05:43.656
Now, that's a king.

886
01:06:25.364 --> 01:06:27.630
We should go.

887
01:06:27.632 --> 01:06:30.566
Oh, no.

888
01:06:39.744 --> 01:06:42.012
Stormfly!

889
01:06:57.829 --> 01:07:00.766
Go! Go!

890
01:07:11.643 --> 01:07:13.644
I-I'm sorry, bud.
I-I just...

891
01:07:38.603 --> 01:07:40.737
Son.

892
01:07:41.907 --> 01:07:43.574
You should be asleep.

893
01:07:43.576 --> 01:07:45.878
I was thirsty.

894
01:07:48.981 --> 01:07:50.717
Yeah, come here.

895
01:08:01.960 --> 01:08:04.394
Dad?

896
01:08:04.396 --> 01:08:08.030
Are you gonna get us a new mom?

897
01:08:11.003 --> 01:08:12.735
I don't want another.

898
01:08:12.737 --> 01:08:16.973
Your mom was
the only woman for me.

899
01:08:16.975 --> 01:08:19.645
She was the love of my life.

900
01:08:21.579 --> 01:08:25.782
But with love comes loss, son.

901
01:08:25.784 --> 01:08:27.651
It's part of the deal.

902
01:08:27.653 --> 01:08:32.391
Sometimes it hurts, but
in the end, it's all worth it.

903
01:08:35.094 --> 01:08:38.562
There's no greater gift
than love.

904
01:09:20.872 --> 01:09:23.139
It's okay, bud.

905
01:09:23.141 --> 01:09:25.545
You belong there, with her.

906
01:09:27.246 --> 01:09:28.745
We don't.

907
01:09:31.115 --> 01:09:34.550
And that's all right.

908
01:09:34.552 --> 01:09:36.853
We'll find a way to man...

909
01:09:46.030 --> 01:09:47.697
Hey!

910
01:09:48.868 --> 01:09:52.635
She followed us back!

911
01:09:55.940 --> 01:09:59.077
We might not have to
say good-bye after all.

912
01:10:06.551 --> 01:10:07.884
That's it.

913
01:10:07.886 --> 01:10:09.686
Woo-hoo! Yeah!

914
01:10:09.688 --> 01:10:11.722
- Ruffnut?
- Miss me?

915
01:10:11.724 --> 01:10:13.190
How did you escape?

916
01:10:13.192 --> 01:10:14.924
I annoyed them
till they let me go.

917
01:10:14.926 --> 01:10:16.593
Wait. Wait.

918
01:10:16.595 --> 01:10:19.696
- Grimmel let you go?
- So dumb.

919
01:10:19.698 --> 01:10:21.697
They couldn't handle me.

920
01:10:21.699 --> 01:10:23.700
See, everyone thinks
Tuffnut's more annoying, but...

921
01:10:23.702 --> 01:10:26.003
- Wait, hold on.
- Ruffnut, focus.

922
01:10:26.005 --> 01:10:27.870
Were you followed?

923
01:10:27.872 --> 01:10:29.940
I never look back, Hiccup.

924
01:10:29.942 --> 01:10:32.041
Toothless.

925
01:10:32.043 --> 01:10:34.544
Toothless!

926
01:10:45.690 --> 01:10:47.493
Toothless, come back!

927
01:10:55.935 --> 01:10:57.270
No!

928
01:11:13.918 --> 01:11:18.754
And now our little game
must come to an end.

929
01:11:23.028 --> 01:11:24.894
Call them off, alpha!

930
01:11:24.896 --> 01:11:27.699
No reason for her to die, too.

931
01:11:40.912 --> 01:11:42.178
What are they doing?

932
01:11:42.180 --> 01:11:45.915
- They could totally take him.
- Not with her life on the line.

933
01:11:49.121 --> 01:11:50.687
Save your breath.

934
01:11:50.689 --> 01:11:53.991
The only alpha
they respond to is me.

935
01:11:58.963 --> 01:12:00.897
Oh...

936
01:12:00.899 --> 01:12:03.799
don't feel too badly.
You tried your best.

937
01:12:03.801 --> 01:12:08.705
But you are nothing
without your dragon.

938
01:12:23.788 --> 01:12:25.155
Toothless!

939
01:12:43.074 --> 01:12:45.308
Oh, that is
just great!

940
01:12:45.310 --> 01:12:46.476
Now what?

941
01:12:46.478 --> 01:12:50.046
I think it's time for number
two to become number one.

942
01:12:50.048 --> 01:12:51.984
He'll listen to you.

943
01:12:56.988 --> 01:12:59.255
- Don't say it.
- I wasn't going to.

944
01:12:59.257 --> 01:13:00.991
I shouldn't have
dragged you out there.

945
01:13:00.993 --> 01:13:03.226
He wouldn't have flown me back.
She wouldn't have followed.

946
01:13:03.228 --> 01:13:05.227
Yep.

947
01:13:05.229 --> 01:13:08.197
I feel like the same screwup
I was before I met Toothless.

948
01:13:08.199 --> 01:13:10.032
I can see that.

949
01:13:10.034 --> 01:13:12.201
Are you just gonna stand there
and agree with everything?

950
01:13:12.203 --> 01:13:13.035
Well, you're right.

951
01:13:13.037 --> 01:13:15.871
You're back
to where you started,

952
01:13:15.873 --> 01:13:18.208
but I was the first
to believe in you.

953
01:13:18.210 --> 01:13:19.910
And I have watched you doubt

954
01:13:19.912 --> 01:13:22.379
whether you're worthy
ever since.

955
01:13:22.381 --> 01:13:24.214
But you know what?

956
01:13:24.216 --> 01:13:28.085
I am the person I am today
because of you.

957
01:13:28.087 --> 01:13:31.153
I never told you that,
but it's true.

958
01:13:31.155 --> 01:13:33.857
You are the bravest,
most stubborn,

959
01:13:33.859 --> 01:13:37.861
most determined knucklehead
I know.

960
01:13:37.863 --> 01:13:40.129
Toothless didn't
give you that, Hiccup.

961
01:13:40.131 --> 01:13:43.467
- He just made it...
- Easier.

962
01:13:43.469 --> 01:13:47.070
And now it's gonna be
a lot harder.

963
01:13:47.072 --> 01:13:50.507
So, what are you
gonna do about it?

964
01:13:50.509 --> 01:13:53.242
Probably something stupid.

965
01:13:53.244 --> 01:13:56.015
That's the Hiccup I know.

966
01:13:59.118 --> 01:14:02.018
Suit up, gang.
We're going to get them back.

967
01:14:02.020 --> 01:14:05.021
- What?
- He's lost his mind.

968
01:14:05.023 --> 01:14:08.125
Now, that's marriage material.

969
01:14:08.127 --> 01:14:11.361
At last, faithful pupil,
you are ready.

970
01:14:11.363 --> 01:14:16.532
Um, how are we gonna get our
dragons back without dragons?

971
01:14:16.534 --> 01:14:17.901
Trust me.

972
01:14:21.506 --> 01:14:23.973
- Watch yourselves.
- You're next.

973
01:14:25.543 --> 01:14:26.910
Move it.

974
01:14:29.782 --> 01:14:32.048
Um, that's right, alpha.

975
01:14:32.050 --> 01:14:34.020
No surprises.

976
01:14:42.394 --> 01:14:47.964
So, jump off the cliff
in these.

977
01:14:47.966 --> 01:14:49.465
That's the best you've got?

978
01:14:49.467 --> 01:14:52.268
No, you guys are
the best I've got.

979
01:14:52.270 --> 01:14:54.537
Aw.

980
01:14:54.539 --> 01:14:56.305
- I'm with him! Who else?!
- I'm with...

981
01:14:56.307 --> 01:14:58.340
Ruffnut, that was my line.

982
01:14:58.342 --> 01:15:00.343
- Let's go!
- Try to keep up!

983
01:15:04.483 --> 01:15:06.049
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

984
01:15:06.051 --> 01:15:08.818
- I'm doing it!
- All right! - Oh!

985
01:15:08.820 --> 01:15:10.085
Get clear!

986
01:15:18.896 --> 01:15:21.197
Aw.

987
01:15:21.199 --> 01:15:23.366
You didn't think I'd actually
hand you the Night Fury,

988
01:15:23.368 --> 01:15:24.366
did you?

989
01:15:24.368 --> 01:15:26.068
He's mine to kill.

990
01:15:26.070 --> 01:15:27.870
That snake!

991
01:15:27.872 --> 01:15:30.574
I intend to finish
what I started.

992
01:15:30.576 --> 01:15:34.910
Best of luck controlling them
without an alpha.

993
01:15:34.912 --> 01:15:37.182
Hold on, Toothless!

994
01:15:40.618 --> 01:15:42.986
Let go!

995
01:15:42.988 --> 01:15:44.486
Could've used
some practice!

996
01:15:44.488 --> 01:15:46.589
Ah, I should've
skipped breakfast!

997
01:15:56.969 --> 01:15:58.401
Toothless!

998
01:16:00.572 --> 01:16:02.973
Look out!

999
01:16:02.975 --> 01:16:05.008
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

1000
01:16:06.912 --> 01:16:10.080
They're getting away!

1001
01:16:19.123 --> 01:16:21.391
Perfect timing.

1002
01:16:21.393 --> 01:16:24.059
- Put that down!
- I'll take the skinny one!

1003
01:16:24.061 --> 01:16:25.061
Game faces!

1004
01:16:25.063 --> 01:16:27.897
Yeah, what are you waiting for?
Get in there.

1005
01:16:27.899 --> 01:16:29.132
Yeah!

1006
01:16:29.134 --> 01:16:31.537
Take that!

1007
01:16:38.377 --> 01:16:40.413
Ah.

1008
01:16:58.229 --> 01:16:59.428
- Watch out!
- The dragons are everywhere!

1009
01:16:59.430 --> 01:17:01.196
- Incoming!
- Here they come!

1010
01:17:01.198 --> 01:17:03.666
Incoming!

1011
01:17:03.668 --> 01:17:05.201
Take cover!

1012
01:17:05.203 --> 01:17:07.437
Where are you going?!

1013
01:17:11.143 --> 01:17:13.943
- Heads up!
- - Thanks.

1014
01:17:13.945 --> 01:17:14.945
Look out!

1015
01:17:18.015 --> 01:17:19.951
Thanks.

1016
01:17:45.077 --> 01:17:47.177
I'm coming, Toothless!

1017
01:17:47.179 --> 01:17:50.280
You still think
he cares about you?

1018
01:17:51.649 --> 01:17:55.487
Let's just see who he follows.

1019
01:18:07.599 --> 01:18:09.732
I'm sorry, bud, for everything.

1020
01:18:28.787 --> 01:18:30.722
Now, let's go get her.

1021
01:18:34.225 --> 01:18:36.625
Woo-hoo! Yeah!

1022
01:18:36.627 --> 01:18:38.160
Number two coming through!

1023
01:18:38.162 --> 01:18:39.728
Surprise!

1024
01:18:39.730 --> 01:18:41.196
Sorry about that.

1025
01:18:41.198 --> 01:18:43.165
Come on.

1026
01:18:44.569 --> 01:18:48.537
- All right!
- One more free! Four to go!

1027
01:18:50.408 --> 01:18:52.442
Try to keep up!

1028
01:18:52.444 --> 01:18:54.744
I got your backs. Oh!

1029
01:18:56.280 --> 01:18:59.348
Yeah, it's almost like
we're a team.

1030
01:19:02.253 --> 01:19:05.287
You brought a baby to a battle.

1031
01:19:05.289 --> 01:19:08.357
Ah-ah-ah. I wouldn't
do that if I were you.

1032
01:19:18.235 --> 01:19:20.702
God, I love that dragon.

1033
01:19:20.704 --> 01:19:23.839
Come on! Come back here!

1034
01:19:25.810 --> 01:19:27.811
Sorry we're late for the party.

1035
01:19:27.813 --> 01:19:29.648
You're right on time.

1036
01:19:39.356 --> 01:19:41.394
That's it. That's it.

1037
01:19:52.369 --> 01:19:55.104
How are we gonna get him off
her back without hurting her?

1038
01:19:55.106 --> 01:19:57.440
Fear the facial hair!

1039
01:20:06.350 --> 01:20:07.884
- Oh, I have missed this.
- Me, too.

1040
01:20:07.886 --> 01:20:09.885
Oh!

1041
01:20:09.887 --> 01:20:11.487
Ooh. See that there?

1042
01:20:11.489 --> 01:20:13.522
Aw. Cute.

1043
01:20:13.524 --> 01:20:16.326
That's a bad omen.
You're cursed.

1044
01:20:22.466 --> 01:20:24.233
Yes! Go on!

1045
01:20:24.235 --> 01:20:25.501
Good on you!

1046
01:20:25.503 --> 01:20:27.836
I guess you're not
so bad after all.

1047
01:20:50.494 --> 01:20:52.528
Abandon ship!

1048
01:20:52.530 --> 01:20:54.397
Whoa!

1049
01:21:01.840 --> 01:21:03.205
- Yay!
- Oh, that was awesome!

1050
01:21:03.207 --> 01:21:06.276
Yeah!

1051
01:21:10.814 --> 01:21:13.751
Uh, we've got problems.

1052
01:21:28.466 --> 01:21:31.670
Take him down, Hiccup!

1053
01:21:40.744 --> 01:21:43.515
We need a better plan,
and quick!

1054
01:21:47.886 --> 01:21:50.320
Uh, uh, what are,
what are you doing?

1055
01:21:50.322 --> 01:21:53.723
Okay. Okay.

1056
01:22:02.466 --> 01:22:03.967
Where has he gone?

1057
01:22:19.350 --> 01:22:20.849
You'll kill both of us!

1058
01:22:20.851 --> 01:22:23.318
Fighting over a dragon?

1059
01:22:23.320 --> 01:22:24.754
That's your plan?

1060
01:22:27.792 --> 01:22:30.393
This is.

1061
01:22:33.530 --> 01:22:35.466
Save him.

1062
01:23:11.603 --> 01:23:13.905
No!

1063
01:23:19.610 --> 01:23:21.009
See?

1064
01:23:21.011 --> 01:23:23.381
I knew you'd come around.

1065
01:23:42.966 --> 01:23:44.802
Yeah!

1066
01:23:59.050 --> 01:24:01.049
Hey. Good morning, bud.

1067
01:24:03.054 --> 01:24:05.655
Here you go.

1068
01:24:05.657 --> 01:24:08.458
Boy, you're full of surprises.

1069
01:24:09.860 --> 01:24:12.894
He's all yours.

1070
01:24:24.042 --> 01:24:26.642
You know, Eret may be
blessed with brawn,

1071
01:24:26.644 --> 01:24:30.545
but, just between us,
you have the brains.

1072
01:24:30.547 --> 01:24:32.815
Number one.

1073
01:25:04.615 --> 01:25:07.485
You're right, bud.
It's time.

1074
01:25:09.154 --> 01:25:14.022
I was so busy fighting for
a world that I wanted,

1075
01:25:14.024 --> 01:25:17.061
I didn't think about
what you needed.

1076
01:25:20.164 --> 01:25:23.766
You've looked after us
for long enough.

1077
01:25:23.768 --> 01:25:25.938
Time to look after yourselves.

1078
01:25:39.583 --> 01:25:42.919
Oh, Stormfly, my good girl.

1079
01:25:42.921 --> 01:25:44.187
All right, Grumpy.

1080
01:25:44.189 --> 01:25:47.190
Off you go.

1081
01:25:47.192 --> 01:25:50.492
So long, you big ugly beast.

1082
01:25:50.494 --> 01:25:51.693
I'll miss you.

1083
01:26:00.505 --> 01:26:03.108
Oh, Cloudjumper. Oh.

1084
01:26:11.850 --> 01:26:13.849
Go on, bud.

1085
01:26:13.851 --> 01:26:16.018
Lead them to the Hidden World.

1086
01:26:17.956 --> 01:26:20.156
You'll be safe there.

1087
01:26:20.158 --> 01:26:23.659
Safer than you could
ever be with me.

1088
01:26:24.828 --> 01:26:26.829
It's okay.
I love you, too.

1089
01:26:26.831 --> 01:26:28.531
And I want you to be free.

1090
01:26:32.203 --> 01:26:34.903
Our world doesn't deserve you.

1091
01:26:34.905 --> 01:26:36.175
Yet.

1092
01:26:47.585 --> 01:26:49.020
Go, Toothless.

1093
01:26:51.088 --> 01:26:52.724
Go.

1094
01:29:19.002 --> 01:29:21.736
To the chief and chieftess!

1095
01:29:21.738 --> 01:29:24.305
Yeah!

1096
01:29:24.307 --> 01:29:26.208
Good on you!

1097
01:29:26.210 --> 01:29:29.678
Come, cry into
my full, thick beard.

1098
01:29:29.680 --> 01:29:31.946
It's so beautiful!

1099
01:29:31.948 --> 01:29:34.183
Gross.

1100
01:29:34.185 --> 01:29:36.352
Okay, you win.

1101
01:29:36.354 --> 01:29:38.853
I like sensitive guys.

1102
01:29:38.855 --> 01:29:40.690
I thought
it would never happen.

1103
01:29:40.692 --> 01:29:42.223
Finally, right?

1104
01:30:12.457 --> 01:30:15.090
<i>There were dragons
when I was a boy.</i>

1105
01:30:18.095 --> 01:30:20.428
<i>Ah, there were
great, grim sky dragons</i>

1106
01:30:20.430 --> 01:30:24.500
<i>that nested on the clifftops
like gigantic, scary birds.</i>

1107
01:30:25.869 --> 01:30:27.335
<i>Little, brown, scuttly dragons</i>

1108
01:30:27.337 --> 01:30:31.941
<i>that hunted down the mice and
rats in well-organized packs.</i>

1109
01:30:31.943 --> 01:30:34.375
<i>Preposterously huge sea dragons</i>

1110
01:30:34.377 --> 01:30:39.348
<i>that were 20 times as big
as the big blue whale.</i>

1111
01:30:39.350 --> 01:30:41.851
<i>Some say they crawled
back into the sea,</i>

1112
01:30:41.853 --> 01:30:45.454
<i>leaving not a bone nor a fang
for men to remember them by.</i>

1113
01:30:45.456 --> 01:30:50.159
<i>Others say they were nothing
but folktales to begin with.</i>

1114
01:30:50.161 --> 01:30:52.698
<i>Ah, I'm okay with that.</i>

1115
01:31:13.850 --> 01:31:15.918
Hey.

1116
01:31:15.920 --> 01:31:18.256
Hey there, bud.

1117
01:31:24.828 --> 01:31:26.331
Remember me?

1118
01:31:28.800 --> 01:31:30.435
It's okay.

1119
01:31:40.077 --> 01:31:44.045
Hey, I am glad
to see you, too, bud.

1120
01:31:44.047 --> 01:31:46.482
He's not gonna eat your father.

1121
01:31:46.484 --> 01:31:48.483
Hey!

1122
01:31:48.485 --> 01:31:50.318
How's the tail holding up?

1123
01:31:50.320 --> 01:31:52.153
Probably could use some oil
and a little fine-tuning.

1124
01:31:52.155 --> 01:31:55.089
Look, it's okay.
They're friends.

1125
01:31:57.295 --> 01:32:00.528
Cut it out.

1126
01:32:00.530 --> 01:32:01.930
Here.

1127
01:32:01.932 --> 01:32:03.566
Go on. It's all right.

1128
01:32:03.568 --> 01:32:05.500
Come.

1129
01:32:05.502 --> 01:32:07.937
He won't hurt you.

1130
01:32:07.939 --> 01:32:09.604
Hold your hands out.

1131
01:32:09.606 --> 01:32:12.141
Like this.

1132
01:32:12.143 --> 01:32:14.045
That's it.

1133
01:32:16.447 --> 01:32:18.984
Let him come to you.

1134
01:33:12.369 --> 01:33:14.370
<i>Legend says that</i>

1135
01:33:14.372 --> 01:33:17.138
<i>when the ground quakes
or lava spews from the earth,</i>

1136
01:33:17.140 --> 01:33:22.244
<i>it's the dragons, letting us
know they're still here,</i>

1137
01:33:22.246 --> 01:33:25.182
<i>waiting for us to figure out
how to get along.</i>

1138
01:33:32.689 --> 01:33:35.691
<i>Yes, the world believes
the dragons are gone,</i>

1139
01:33:35.693 --> 01:33:38.393
<i>if they ever existed at all.</i>

1140
01:33:38.395 --> 01:33:43.398
<i>But we Berkians,
we know otherwise.</i>

1141
01:33:43.400 --> 01:33:46.567
<i>And we'll guard this secret
until the time comes</i>

1142
01:33:46.569 --> 01:33:50.571
<i>when dragons can return
in peace.</i>

1143
01:33:53.470 --> 01:33:58.470
Subtitles by <font color="#ff0000">explosiveskull</font>
